      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Ongoing pain after total hip replacement is a source of frustration to both the patient and the surgeon. A structured approach to the evaluation of patients with postoperative pain is essential. The key to such an approach is a meticulous patient history and physical examination. The results of relevant investigations allow an effective treatment plan to be quickly implemented."},
